WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.134
The host launches two blocks of thirty-two

00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:05.391
GPU threads. The arrays have thirty-three

00:00:05.391 --> 00:00:08.025
elements, so some threads have no element

00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:08.777
to write.

00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:15.787
Each thread calculates its global index.

00:00:15.787 --> 00:00:18.716
In block one, thread zero gets thirty-two.

00:00:18.716 --> 00:00:20.808
The next thread gets thirty-three.

00:00:25.308 --> 00:00:27.636
The bounds check compares each index with

00:00:27.636 --> 00:00:29.631
thirty-three. Which of these two threads

00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:30.961
enters the if block?

00:00:39.461 --> 00:00:42.115
Thread zero writes ninety-nine at index

00:00:42.115 --> 00:00:44.327
thirty-two. Thread one skips the

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:46.539
assignment because index thirty-three is

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:47.866
outside the arrays.
